# Every arrowhead at once, plus a flaming one. The buff is the small half (15%
# final damage and 20% attack for 40 seconds); the flaming arrows are all the
# damage.
#
# One trigger fires six arrows, each one attack of nine lines on six enemies,
# one after another. GMS's "Duration: 5 sec." is how long an arrow hunts for a
# target, which is why namuwiki praises it for farming. Namu gives the total,
# 534,600%, which is exactly 6 arrows x 18 volleys x 9 lines x 550%.
#
# It has eighteen volleys on a 2-second re-trigger, so it runs out at 36 seconds
# of the 40-second buff; the tooltip itself warns the attack stops while the
# buff is still up. GMS fires it "upon attack", and this game's swing never
# pauses, so that is simply every 2 seconds.
#
# The attack % goes in the same pool as Marksmanship's. GMS writes this one as
# indiePadR and Marksmanship's as padR, but this game has one pool, and
# namuwiki's table also sums the pair to 45%.
name: "Quiver Barrage"
description:
  "Fire every type of arrowhead at once, including a special flaming arrowhead "
  "that explodes when it hits an enemy. The Flaming Arrow targets the boss "
  "with the highest HP first and is unaffected by attack reflection. The "
  "Flaming Arrow is prepared in limited quantities and will no longer attack "
  "once used up."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ACTIVE
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_BOW_MASTER_V skill_order: 3 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_JOB
max_level: 30
base_delay_ms: 120
cooldown_seconds: 120.0
buff {
  duration_seconds: 40.0
  base { final_dmg_pct: 0.15 attack_pct: 0.055 }
  per_level { attack_pct: 0.005 }
  pulse {
    label: "Flaming Arrow"
    cast_interval_seconds: 2.0
    casts: 6
    max_enemies: 6
    lines: 9
    max_pulses: 18
    base { skill_pct: 2.60 }
    per_level { skill_pct: 0.10 }
  }
}
